Pin the DatePicker samples' date.

WHY: the same defect as 0001, one file over and with a 24-hour period instead of a one-minute one —
upstream seeds these with `LocalDate.now()`, so the renders change at midnight. Slower to show up
than the TimePicker flake and identical in kind; `DatePickerFutureOnlySample` is the worst of the
three because its `minValidDate` bound moves too, greying out a different set of wheel cells each
day.

PINNED TO `:catalog`'s OWN INSTANT (2026-01-01), for the reason 0001 gives.

A renderer limitation rather than an upstream bug: `LocalDate.now()` is right for a sample someone
runs on a watch, and wrong for one captured as a still.

